@@ -1,5 +1,25 @@
 # Changelog
 
+## 0.9.3
+
+- Renewal dates are counted from the anchor, so a customer anchored on the 31st goes
+  back to the 31st after a short month (this is what 0.2.1 promised).
+- The change day counts as time left in proration, as `docs/proration.md` says. Credits
+  on a plan change or cancellation are based on what was paid for the current charge,
+  after discount and earlier credits, at the tax rate it was billed at.
+- Amounts are read, formatted, exported and put on statements with the currency's own
+  number of decimals (JPY 0, KWD 3).
+- Splits (`allocate`) are exact and fair, and tax on an invoice is worked out per rate
+  and then spread over the lines, so lines add up to the totals.
+- Credit notes are limited to the net actually charged, with tax taken as a share of
+  the line's tax. Credit lines on later invoices count against the original charge.
+- Credit notes refund cash only up to the cash received; the rest goes to account credit.
+- Account credit is applied to an invoice after tax and no longer changes its lines.
+- Plan changes keep scheduled changes and do not use up a coupon period.
+- Invoice numbers are only used once an invoice exists, so there are no gaps.
+- Revenue and tax reports ignore credit notes in other currencies.
+- Documentation: the default rounding mode is half-even (since 0.4.0); proration page
+  describes how the credit is worked out.
 ## 0.9.2
 
 - Statements list payments and write-offs.
